    "bugs": {
      "18938": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "is_markdown": true,
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "time": "2025-08-21T21:42:41Z",
            "attachment_id": {},
            "count": 0,
            "text": "c.f.\n\n```\nseq(as.Date(\"2025-01-01\"), \"2025-01-07\")\n# [1] \"2025-01-01\" \"2025-01-02\" \"2025-01-03\" \"2025-01-04\" \"2025-01-05\" \"2025-01-06\" \"2025-01-07\"\n\n## vs.\n\nseq(as.Date(\"2025-01-01\"), \"2025-01-07\", by=1)\n# Error in seq.int(from = unclass(from), to = unclass(to), by = by) : \n#   'to' must be a finite number\n# In addition: Warning message:\n# In seq.Date(as.Date(\"2025-01-01\"), \"2025-01-07\", by = 1) :\n#   NAs introduced by coercion\n```\n\nI think automatic conversion to `Date` is quite appealing, much like `DateVector >= \"2025-01-01\"` 'just works', so it would be good to have it supported.",
            "bug_id": 18938,
            "creation_time": "2025-08-21T21:42:41Z",
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 102061,
            "tags": []
          },
          {
            "text": "For \"ragged\" (not equally-spaced) `by=`, we already have `as.POSIXlt` coercion so this works too:\n\n```\nseq(as.Date('2025-01-01'), '2025-08-01', by='month')\n# [1] \"2025-01-01\" \"2025-02-01\" \"2025-03-01\" \"2025-04-01\" \"2025-05-01\" \"2025-06-01\" \"2025-07-01\" \"2025-08-01\"\n```",
            "bug_id": 18938,
            "count": 1,
            "creation_time": "2025-08-21T21:49:26Z",
            "id": 102062,
            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "is_markdown": true,
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "time": "2025-08-21T21:49:26Z",
            "attachment_id": {}
          },
          {
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "creation_time": "2025-08-21T22:01:15Z",
            "count": 2,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "text": "For the POSIXt case, the simple case is already unsupported, so adding such support would be a separate task IMO:\n\n```\nseq(Sys.time(), '2025-08-22 00:00:00')\n# Error in seq.POSIXt(Sys.time(), \"2025-08-22 00:00:00\") : \n#   exactly three of 'to', 'from', 'by' and 'length.out' / 'along.with' must be specified\nseq(Sys.time(), '2025-10-22 00:00:00', by='months')\n# Error in seq.POSIXt(Sys.time(), \"2025-10-22 00:00:00\", by = \"months\") : \n#   'to' must be a \"POSIXt\" object\n```",
            "bug_id": 18938,
            "attachment_id": {},
            "tags": [],
            "is_private": false,
            "time": "2025-08-21T22:01:15Z",
            "id": 102063
          },
          {
            "text": "Created attachment 3528\nUse as.Date() coercion in more places in seq.Date\n\nHere's one approach.\n\nI'm fairly confident we could drop the `as.Date()` coercion when `from` or `to` are missing -- there, S3 dispatch should guarantee the one `from`/`to` argument present inherits from Date.\n\nKept here for transparency/clarity.\n\nTesting on GHA:\n\nhttps://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/207",
            "bug_id": 18938,
            "count": 3,
            "creation_time": "2025-08-21T22:07:21Z",
            "id": 102064,
            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "is_markdown": true,
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "time": "2025-08-21T22:07:21Z",
            "attachment_id": 3528
          },
          {
            "attachment_id": 3529,
            "tags": [],
            "time": "2025-08-21T22:10:57Z",
            "id": 102065,
            "is_private": false,
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "creation_time": "2025-08-21T22:10:57Z",
            "text": "Created attachment 3529\nUse as.Date() coercion in more places in seq.Date\n\nAdded more tests.",
            "bug_id": 18938,
            "count": 4,
            "is_markdown": true
          },
          {
            "is_markdown": true,
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "time": "2025-08-21T22:17:03Z",
            "attachment_id": {},
            "count": 5,
            "bug_id": 18938,
            "text": "Note that we also have the following working today:\n\n```r\nseq(as.Date('2025-08-01'), 20307, by=1)\n# [1] \"2025-08-01\" \"2025-08-02\" \"2025-08-03\" \"2025-08-04\" \"2025-08-05\" \"2025-08-06\" \"2025-08-07\"\nseq(as.Date('2025-08-01'), '20307', by=1)\n# [1] \"2025-08-01\" \"2025-08-02\" \"2025-08-03\" \"2025-08-04\" \"2025-08-05\" \"2025-08-06\" \"2025-08-07\"\n```\n\nIt seems like a way to write confusing code, so I won't add any associated tests. But at least the former will continue to work under the proposed patch (which is more plausibly useful) because we have since \"recently\" `as.Date(20307)` works. The latter usage will be broken by my proposal, which I think is fine, but still want to call out the potential back-incompatibility.",
            "creation_time": "2025-08-21T22:17:03Z",
            "is_private": false,
            "id": 102066,
            "tags": []
          },
          {
            "creation_time": "2025-08-21T23:46:02Z",
            "text": "Created attachment 3530\nUse as.Date() coercion in more places in seq.Date\n\nDeleted this test:\n\n```\n  identical(seq(as.Date(from_str), \"2025-10-01\", by=\"months\"),\n            seq(as.Date(from_str), as.Date(\"2025-10-01\"), by=\"months\"))\n```\n\nWhile it's indeed a good & useful test, it fails on GHA, from what I can tell due to timezone issues:\n\n```\nWarning in .check_tzones(e1, e2) : 'tzone' attributes are inconsistent\nError: identical(seq(as.Date(from_str), \"2025-10-01\", by = \"months\"),  .... is not TRUE\n```\n\nSince that's related to code that's not touched in the current patch, and I'm not reproducing it locally, I'll defer it to future work.",
            "bug_id": 18938,
            "count": 6,
            "tags": [],
            "id": 102067,
            "is_private": false,
            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "is_markdown": true,
            "attachment_id": 3530,
            "time": "2025-08-21T23:46:02Z"
          },
          {
            "tags": [],
            "attachment_id": {},
            "is_private": false,
            "time": "2026-01-14T15:35:37Z",
            "id": 102568,
            "creator": "aakriti.kushwaha.ak",
            "creation_time": "2026-01-14T15:35:37Z",
            "count": 7,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "text": "Hi,\n\nI noticed that seq.Date behaves inconsistently when the 'to' argument is a string. \nI created a small test file that reproduces the behavior:\n\n- seq(as.Date(\"2025-01-01\"), \"2025-01-07\") works\n- seq(as.Date(\"2025-01-01\"), \"2025-01-07\", by = 1) fails\n\nThis test file can be used to reproduce the issue and help with investigating a potential fix. \nI've attached the file below.\n\nThanks!",
            "bug_id": 18938
          },
          {
            "text": "Created attachment 3597\nSimple test showing Bug 18938: seq.Date fails when ‘to’ is a string with by=1\n\nAttaching a simple test case for Bug 18938. \nIt demonstrates the current inconsistent behavior of seq.Date with string 'to' values.",
            "bug_id": 18938,
            "count": 8,
